---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";

const effectiveDate = "September 14, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply when you use teacher.dev tools."
  compactContent
>
  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">
      Terms of Service
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <div class="border-l-4 border-slate-300 bg-slate-50 p-5">
        <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900">The short version</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These are free tools for teachers, offered as-is. Your files stay
          yours and stay in your Google Drive. Don't use the tools to break the
          law or to harm anyone. We can't promise the service will always be
          available.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. What these terms cover</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These terms apply when you use teacher.dev and its subdomains,
          including the sign-in and authorization service at auth.teacher.dev.
          By using the service you agree to them. If you don't agree, please
          don't use it.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Our <a
            href="/privacy"
            class="font-semibold text-slate-900 underline underline-offset-4 decoration-2"
            >Privacy Policy</a
          > explains how we handle your data and is part of these terms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. Who can use it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          teacher.dev is intended for educators and other adults. It is not
          directed to children. You need a Google account to sign in, and you
          are responsible for keeping that account secure. Anyone who can access
          your Google account can access what you have connected here.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">
          3. Your files and your Google account
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Your files are yours. Connecting Google Drive grants access only to
          files you explicitly select, and only so the tools can do what you
          asked them to do. It grants us no ownership of your content and no
          license to use it for anything else.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You can withdraw that access at any time by disconnecting in the app,
          or at
          <a
            href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions"
            class="font-semibold text-slate-900 underline underline-offset-4 decoration-2"
            >myaccount.google.com/permissions</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          You are responsible for having the right to use the files you connect,
          and for following any rules your school or district places on student
          information.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Please don't:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
          <li>Use the service to break the law or to violate someone's rights</li>
          <li>
            Try to access accounts, data, or systems that don't belong to you
          </li>
          <li>
            Probe, scan, overload, or interfere with the service or the
            infrastructure it runs on
          </li>
          <li>
            Resell the service, or use it to build a competing product from our
            infrastructure
          </li>
          <li>
            Upload or connect content that is malicious, or that you have no
            right to share
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">5. Availability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          teacher.dev is offered free of charge and without a service level
          guarantee. It may be unavailable, interrupted, or changed at any time.
          Features may be added, altered, or removed. We may suspend or
          discontinue the service entirely.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Keep your own copies of anything you care about. Your files live in
          your Google Drive and are not dependent on us, which is deliberate.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">6. Ending it</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          You can stop using teacher.dev whenever you like, and delete your
          account from within the app. We may suspend or end access if these
          terms are being broken, or if we stop offering the service. When your
          account is deleted, connected permissions are revoked at Google and
          your stored account data is removed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">
          7. No warranties
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties
          of any kind, whether express or implied, including any implied
          warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or
          non-infringement. We do not warrant that the service will be
          uninterrupted, timely, secure, or error-free.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">
          8. Limitation of liability
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, teacher.dev and the people who
          build it will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data, profits,
          or goodwill, arising out of your use of or inability to use the
          service.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, so parts of this
          section may not apply to you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">9. Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          teacher.dev works with Google services, and your use of those is
          governed by Google's own terms and policies. We are not responsible
          for Google's services, and changes on their side may affect what these
          tools can do.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">10. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may update these terms. When we do, we will change the effective
          date above. If a change is significant, we will make a reasonable
          effort to tell you. Continuing to use the service after a change means
          you accept the updated terms.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">11. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Questions about these terms can go to
          <a
            href="mailto:support@teacher.dev"
            class="font-semibold text-slate-900 underline underline-offset-4 decoration-2"
            >support@teacher.dev</a
          >.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
